Answer: 70</think>The condition is that \(b+7\) divides \(9b+7\). Since \(9b+7 = 9(b+7) - 56\), we need \(b+7 \mid 56\). For \(b>9\), \(b+7>16\), so the only divisors of 56 greater than 16 are 28 and 56, giving \(b=21\) and \(b=49\). Their sum is \(21+49=70\).

Answer: 70
